Paige Bailey (@DynamicWebPaige) shares that NanoBanana 2 Lite is now her go-to for image generation and editing, offering very high quality at a small fraction of the cost of other models.

She also notes that Omni is now available via the API, enabling automation of creating and editing videos with natural language, not just images. A video demonstration is linked.

@GoogleDeepMind announces two major releases: Nano Banana 2 Lite, the fastest and cheapest Gemini Image model, and Gemini Omni Flash, now accessible through the Gemini API and Google AI Studio to help developers generate and edit high-quality videos.

The Flash-Lite series is an absolute powerhouse. Blazing fast, capable of understanding video, images, and audio, and extremely cost effective.

Paige Bailey has been using Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite for all her personal projects and is looking forward to upgrading to 3.5 Flash-Lite.

@OfficialLoganK: "I am very excited about Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite, our smallest and fastest Gemini model. It is more intelligent in many cases than Gemini 3, has the same cost and is smarter than Gemini 2.5 Flash, which is approaching end of life. It also outpaces 3.1 Flash-Lite on most use cases."
